From 7ba425aefce0e38a1c34095ad15e0211c90066f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 17:36:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/44] docs: drop proposal section citations from source
 comments

Section numbers rot: the 2026-08-20 revision renumbered inference 6.3 -> 6.2,
unchecked 6.4 -> 6.3, and moved conversions and adapt into section 8, which
invalidated 130 citations at a stroke. The comments now state the rule they
depend on instead of pointing at where it is written.

Comment text only -- verified by token comparison (no code changed in any of
the 37 files) and by an indentation check (no comment layout changed). The
first attempt at this was a whole-file regex whose tidy rule deleted every
empty parameter list in 60 files; it was reverted uncommitted, and the script
now edits only inside comments and only tidies lines a citation left behind.

Build clean; CheckedExceptions 83/83.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
